00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.440
He walks behind the table, the other guy walks in front of the table.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:02.560
The other guy being Tom Hanks.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.640
N: And if you look really closely you can totally see the mask fringing on the table.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.360
W: Oh, yeah, dude, we're right!
N: Yep.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:13.440
C: So they had to recreate the stumps essentially, right?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.780
N: Just, all in all, excellent, excellent CG work, but there's little touches like,

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.800
'Oh, lets have him swing his legs to where there's a table',

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.640
That just brings the world together and really, like, drives home the fact that like,

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.080
this character does not have legs.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.480
N: So this one.. have you guys seen this movie before? 
W: Wait, is this the... is this...

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.380
Spider-Man, 1932?

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.500
N: Pleasantville.
W: PLEASANTVILLE! That's it.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:40.340
N: The general premise of this movie is that, 
Peter Parker here has gone back in time -

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:43.360
He's gone back to like an idyllic 'Leave It to Beaver' style TV Show -

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:48.160
and he's basically broadening everyone's horizons, introducing them to modern America.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:52.000
She's embarrassed that she's become colorized because she's becoming modernized -

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.480
She's becoming a modern woman,
 but she doesn't want her husband to see her that way.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.360
So, she needs to have her face painted back to black and white.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:04.420
W: So is it like,- what is he like putting on like green screen makeup and they're just coloring it to be silver?

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.240
N: You got it.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.540
So all they're doing is putting a green screen key on it,

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:13.080
- and desaturating it and that's all they're doing. 
W: You could do this in DaVinci Resolve.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.940
N: I don't know how they did this. The world is black and white

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:23.389
How do they get yellow light to shine on the characters and things in the world? 
C: Well, they're not filming in black and white

00:11:23.389 --> 00:11:24.700
W: I haven't seen any yellow light yet

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.380
N: All right, so the yellow light on the fence there

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.980
You see that? The yellow light on the black? The black and white tree has yellow light on it.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.980
C: Yeah, that's because they're not they're not filming in black and white

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:37.459
W: Yellow reflections on that truck. All right. Is this the results of a clever magic trick?

